-- R43 - PROCESS CHECKS (A23 sweep)
-- Source: thread "Pick ChatGPT tasks for spare capacity", owner's yes on the decision card 27 Nov 2026 21:50 SGT.
-- Proposed 27 Nov 2026; applies Sun 29 Nov 2026 20:00 SGT unless opposed ("oppose R43"); "revert R43" removes it.
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "PROCESS CHECKS: EV after costs, a named p event, an option terms line and a common-shock line on every card and in the BOOK CHECK", "body": "PROCESS CHECKS FROM THE A23 SWEEP (owner's yes of 27 Nov 2026 on the decision card \"Draft the four A23 process items as a rule for Sunday?\"; source: ChatGPT Astra task A23, 120 practitioner and regulator sources, verified by Claude, project files astra_results/VERIFICATION_round7_27nov2026.md). Four additions to every card and to the BOOK CHECK, in both books. They change prints and the EV gate's input, not the exit rules.\n\n1. NET EV AFTER COSTS. Every new card prints \"EV gross <g>R, costs <c>R, net <n>R\". Costs = entry half-spread + exit half-spread + slippage allowance, converted to R with the card's stop distance (option card: premium = 1R, so cost = bid/offer half-width in premium terms over the premium). Until live fills exist, use this default table (round-trip, estimates, to be replaced by the realised fill table from January): G10 majors spot/forward 1 bp of notional; USDCNH 2 bp; USDKRW, USDTWD, USDINR, USDIDR, USDPHP NDF 4 bp; UST, Bund, JGB, gilt futures 0.3 bp of yield; ACGB/KTB futures 0.5 bp; equity index futures 2 bp; WTI/Brent futures 3 bp; FX options: vanilla G10 0.3 vol each side, Asia or wings 0.6 vol, barriers, one-touches and digitals 1.0 vol equivalent each side, times the option's vega. The R01 entry gate (EV > 0) and the thin-edge band (0 to +0.3R) apply to NET EV. A card whose gross EV passes and net fails prints \"REJECTED ON COSTS (gross <g>R)\"; one that moves into the thin-edge band prints \"THIN EDGE ON COSTS\". The no-chase check at fill is unchanged.\n\n2. NAMED p EVENT. Every card prints \"p event: <event>, by <date/time SGT>, graded on <source>\". Linear cards: target before stop under the v15 exits (target on touch, stop on hourly close). Option cards name exactly one of: touch of <level> by expiry (observation source and window), finish beyond <strike> at the <cut> cut, or premium reaching the target before the stop. If one hourly bar carries both target and stop, the outcome is \"indeterminate\" unless the bar order can be shown. R23's calibration cut scores p against this named event only. A card without the line is flagged in the BOOK CHECK as \"p event missing: <card>\".\n\n3. OPTION TERMS LINE. Every barrier, one-touch, no-touch, digital or DNT card prints \"TERMS: <type>, level <x>, observation <continuous|discrete, source>, window <start> to <end> <time zone>, expiry <date> <cut, e.g. NY 10:00>, settlement <cash/physical, currency>\". On paper cards it is the assumed terms and prints \"(paper)\". From the first real-money ticket (January 2027), after the fill the card adds \"TERMS RECONCILED vs confirm: yes\" or \"TERMS MISMATCH: <field>\", and a mismatch is reported in THE BOOK before any other line on that card.\n\n4. COMMON SHOCK LINE. In the weekly BOOK CHECK, and before any new top-tier card, print one line with the book's loss in R across ALL open cards in this book plus every open macro sleeve position (one sleeve line counted as its own R) under three joint shocks: (a) broad USD +2% (DTWEXBGS move applied through each FX card's beta, or 1:1 for USD crosses), (b) risk-off: S&P -5%, VIX +8, UST 10y -20 bp, Asia FX -1.5% vs USD, Brent -6%, (c) US 2y +25 bp with UST 10y +15 bp. Linear cards: move over stop distance; option cards: reprice with the fxopt pricer where it runs (state \"approx delta\" where it does not). Print \"COMMON SHOCK: USD+2% <x>R, risk-off <y>R, 2y+25 <z>R\". If any shock loss is 4R or more, print \"COMMON BET: <shock> <R>\" and any new card that adds to that shock's loss prints one sentence on why the book should carry more of it. No automatic size change: the R31 BOOK BRAKE stays the only sizing rule.\n\nFOOTER: \"R43: costs on <n> cards (<r> rejected, <t> thin on costs); p events <n>/<N>; terms lines <n>/<N options>; common shock max <x>R\".", "rationale": "ChatGPT Astra A23 (27 Nov 2026) swept 120 practitioner, regulator and academic sources for documented process practice and compared 83 practices with our written process; Claude checked the sources (7/8 quotes verbatim on the live page) and our rules. Four gaps: nothing in the rules or spec charges spread, slippage or option bid/offer against EV, so thin-edge cards are overstated; an option card's p is not tied to one event (touch vs terminal vs target-before-stop), so R23 cannot grade it cleanly; there is no barrier/digital terms check before real money in January (observation source, window, cut, settlement); R08 and R14 test pairs of trades, but no line measures the whole book plus the macro sleeve under one joint shock. Drawdown ladder (R31 BOOK BRAKE) and invalidation (R31 VIEW CHANGED) were already covered.", "evidence": "Project files astra_results/VERIFICATION_round7_27nov2026.md; Astra zip astra_A23_process_sweep.zip on Drive (sources.csv, practices.csv, gap_review.csv, top15.md items 2, 3, 4, 5).", "revert_if": "Revert point 1 if, after 30 closed cards, the default costs differ from realised fill costs by more than half (then replace the table instead) or no card changed class; revert point 4 if the line exceeds R33's email budget on two mornings or never moves a decision in 6 weeks.", "review_due": "2027-01-15", "source": "thread"}$j$::jsonb);
